 the web and make distinctions between scholarly and non-scholarly materials. Students will identify a topic and learn search strategies and methods for finding materials in various formats, using information databases such as the library catalog, and print and electronic sources. Assignments will be hands-on and the final product will be an annotated bibliography and a presentation of their research to the class.\u00a0", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Summer.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": ["Read more effectively and efficiently.", "Demonstrate increased ability to apply reading strategies to the text in their college courses.", "Develop more flexibility as a reader.", "Critically think about what they read.", "Recognize different types of text and describe appropriate uses for them."], "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "HE", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2734, "crseId": 363651, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "HE", "catalogNbr": "1105", "titleShort": "College Success-Summer College", "titleLong": "Strategies for College Success: Critical Thinking and Effective Learning", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 1450, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "02:30PM", "timeEnd": "04:00PM", "startDt": "06/24/2019", "endDt": "08/02/2019", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 3, "netid": "hjf4", "firstName": "Heather", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Furnas"}], "pattern": "MTW", "facilityDescr": "Stimson Hall 206", "bldgDescr": "Stimson Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "STM206", "meetingTopicDescr